# Copy to .env and fill in your real keys. Never commit .env.
# Each GEMINI_KEY_N is one provider slot in the router pool. Scale by
# adding GEMINI_KEY_4, _5, etc. — no code change needed.
#
# Each slot should be backed by its own quota bucket. In practice that means
# either (a) one separate Google account per key, or (b) one separate Google
# Cloud project per key (multiple projects can live under one account).
# Multiple keys generated from the SAME project share one quota and won't
# multiply throughput.
GEMINI_KEY_1=
GEMINI_KEY_2=
GEMINI_KEY_3=
